// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/analog/mos_psp103_50c_data.t27 -- the IHP SG13G2 PSP103 current tables at 50 C, corner mos_tt: data and nothing else
; Analog M4b-psp (#10856, epic #10486). M3b (specs/analog/mos_psp103_data.t27) tabulated Id(Vgs, Vds) of sg13_lv_nmos (W 1.0 um, L 0.45 um)
; and sg13_lv_pmos (W 3.0 um, L 0.45 um) at 27 C. The uberWAVE golden SAR deck is simulated at 50 C (`.options TEMP = 50`), and its comparator
; is judged by this milestone against ngspice at that temperature, so the same two tables are printed again at 50 C, the same grid, the
; same units, the same recipe; M3b's file is not edited. Everything hand-written here is the wrapper around the numbers, the pins and the tests.
; -
; WHERE THE NUMBERS COME FROM. ngspice-47 and the IHP-Open-PDK checkout at commit 21133f219b1a6da10d803e345761e77415ceff40: the model file
; ihp-sg13g2/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerMOSlv.lib (PSP 103.6, section mos_tt) with psp103.osdi compiled from the same commit. TNOM is 27 C, the
; circuit temperature 50 C (`.temp 50`). The deck is specs/analog/decks/psp103_tab_tt50.cir, psp103_tab_tt.cir of M3b with that one line changed
; and the held-out set cut to its first 200 points; run as `IHP_PDK=<checkout> IHP_OSDI=<dir with psp103.osdi> ngspice -b psp103_tab_tt50.cir`. As a check
; of the toolchain, the same ngspice and checkout, run on psp103_tab_tt.cir (27 C), reproduce M3b's TT_N, TT_P and TT_R2_N word for word.
; -
; THE GRID AND THE UNITS are M3b's: 25 x 25 nodes, 24 cells of 62.5 mV over 0 .. 1.5 V on each axis, index ix * 25 + iy with ix along Vgs and iy
; along Vds, a unit 2^-24 V, an entry Id * (dt / C) with dt / C = 200 V/A, so one unit is 0.298 nA. For the PMOS the axes are Vsg and Vsd, the source
; and bulk on the 1.5 V rail, and the entry is the current that leaves the drain. Negative entries (the gate current out of the drain at Vds = 0)
; are held at 0. The held-out points are the first 200 of the R2 sequence of M3b (R2_A1, R2_A2 there): never nodes, current in pA.
; -
; WHAT 50 C DOES. The saturation current falls (NMOS 1349912 to 1271348 units, -5.8 %; PMOS 1011527 to 968691, -4.2 %) and the weak inversion
; current rises (NMOS at Vgs = 0.25 V, Vds = 1.5 V: 1725 to 2774 units), the two curves crossing near Vgs = 0.6 V (node 10): the threshold falls
; with temperature and the mobility falls with it. Both tables stay nondecreasing along both axes, zero at Vds = 0, with an off current of at
; most 3 units (the tests below).
; -
; WHAT A PASS SAYS. The numbers in this file are the numbers the deck printed, in order (the pins), the tables are monotone and zero at Vds = 0,
; and the temperature moves them the way it does in the model (the relations above).
; WHAT IT DOES NOT SAY. That these are the tables a board loads (no bitstream here), that the numbers are right (they are ngspice's, at reltol 1e-6,
; vntol 1e-9, abstol 1e-14), anything about another W, L, m, corner or temperature, or about charge: only current is tabulated.
; ASCII only, English only.
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

module AnalogMosPsp10350cData;

use analog::mos_table::{monotone};
use analog::mos_psp103_data::{TT_N, TT_P, fold_arr};

; --- what the numbers are -------------------------------------------------------------------------
pub const KIND : str = "analog-table-data";
pub const ID : str = "analog/mos_psp103_50c_data";
pub const REFERENCE : str = "IHP-Open-PDK ihp-sg13g2 cornerMOSlv.lib (PSP 103.6) through ngspice-47 and OSDI, 50 C";
/// The IHP-Open-PDK checkout every number was made from (the commit of M3b's tables).
pub const PDK_COMMIT : str = "21133f219b1a6da10d803e345761e77415ceff40";
pub const TEMP50_C : u32 = 50;
/// The model's own nominal temperature.
pub const TNOM_C : u32 = 27;
/// How many held-out points a device has.
pub const R2_COUNT_50 : u32 = 200;

; --- order-sensitive folds of the pasted numbers (fold of linear.t27) ----------------------------------------
pub const PIN_TAB50 : u64 = 0xD9CE7524E09487AB;
pub const PIN_HELD50 : u64 = 0xC6BC11B1A4BBAAEF;

